- board = local_assigns.fetch(:board, "ogos")

.alert.alert-light.border
  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goal of this page
  %p.mb-3
    See who is building real OG habits — writing useful OGOs and working goals with check-ins, connections, and completions.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Context
  %p.mb-3
    Real OG Leaders has boards for different clarity practices. Use the tabs to switch boards; the timeframe applies to whichever board is open.
    Observations insights talks about the ratio of
    %strong kudos
    to
    %strong constructive feedback
    OGOs. Goals practice is a steady cadence of confidence checks, linking goals to meaningful work, and completing what you start.

  %h3.fw-semibold.mb-2 Specifics of this page
  - if board == "goals"
    %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Goals board
    %ul.mb-3
      %li
        %strong Confidence checks
        — goal confidence checks reported in the timeframe (hover for count)
      %li
        %strong Connected
        — personal goals linked in the timeframe to a prompt, assignment, ability, aspiration, or a team/department/company goal (not only another personal goal)
      %li
        %strong Completed
        — personal goals completed in the timeframe
      %li
        %i.bi.bi-star-fill.text-warning.me-1
        when all three checks are present
    %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Sort order
    %p.mb-0
      Most confidence checks first, then most connected goals, then most completions, then latest confidence check, then name.
  - else
    %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 OGOs board
    %ul.mb-3
      %li Author of a published, non-journal OGO about someone else (the author is not on the observee list)
      %li At least one qualifying kudos OGO and/or constructive feedback OGO in the selected timeframe
    %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 How to read each row
    %ul.mb-3
      %li
        %i.bi.bi-check-circle-fill.text-success.me-1
        under
        %strong Kudos
        means ≥1 kudos OGO — hover for the count
      %li
        %i.bi.bi-check-circle-fill.text-primary.me-1
        under
        %strong Constructive feedback
        means ≥1 constructive feedback OGO — hover for the count
      %li
        %i.bi.bi-star-fill.text-warning.me-1
        means both checks in this timeframe
    %h5.fw-semibold.mb-2 Sort order
    %p.mb-0
      Both (star) first, then constructive only, then kudos only. Within a group: more total OGOs first, then most recent qualifying OGO, then name.
